# ---- Secrets / env ----
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# ---- Local databases (user memory; contains personal preferences) ----
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Backups too. `*.db` alone does not match `wandergent-memory.db.bak`, and the backup
# holds exactly the personal data the rule above exists to keep out of the repository.
*.bak
*.db.*

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---- IDE / OS ----
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# ---- Android ----
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties
# gradle-wrapper.jar is deliberately NOT ignored: Gradle requires it in the repo,
# or `./gradlew` cannot run on a fresh clone or a CI runner.

# ---- Local-only working files (kept on disk, never published) ----
# Personal job-search material: resume bullets and scripted interview answers.
# Valuable, but it is not project documentation and does not belong to a reader.
docs/resume-highlights.md
# AI-assistant workflow log. Records this machine's layout (install paths, user
# directories) and approvals that mean nothing outside this checkout.
PENDING-APPROVAL.md
# Inward-facing docs. Nothing here is secret; they are written for whoever is building this
# rather than for whoever is reading it, so they stay local. `decisions.md` and `api.md` are
# deliberately NOT in this list -- the reasoning and the client contract are the point.
CLAUDE.md
docs/progress.md
docs/open-issues.md
# Retired baseline: its figures describe a subset and a constraint layer that no longer exist,
# so publishing it would invite someone to read stale numbers as current.
docs/eval-baseline.json
# Raw eval records. Local while the eval is failing; publishing them makes `decisions.md`'s
# eval analysis checkable, which is worth doing once the subset is green again.
docs/eval-runs/

# ---- JVM crash logs ----
hs_err_pid*.log
